#X text 30 70 Alignment is a number from 0 to 8: 0/1/2 are top left \, center and right \, 3/4/5 are the same at the vertical center and 6/7/8 at the bottom. The text is laid out in a box as wide as the object \, starting at the x you give it., f 64;
#X text 30 140 The 'textalign' message sets the alignment used by the text commands that follow \, so you don't have to repeat it., f 64;
#X text 30 482 The 'image' and 'svg' messages draw a file from disk at an x/y position: 'image <path> <x> <y>' and 'svg <path> <x> <y>'. Give them a path to a file next to your patch., f 64;
