#X text 55 22 Each layer keeps its own drawing list and can be redrawn on its own \, which is much cheaper than redrawing everything. The 'layer' message picks the layer that the following commands are added to \, and the following 'bang' renders just that layer., f 69;
#X text 55 76 Layer 0 is the base layer \, drawn straight over the background. Extra layers are numbered from 1 upwards and are drawn on top of it. Use them in order: skipping one makes the object redraw everything instead., f 69;
